WEBVTT

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.230
Seigi-kun.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:15.940
Tanimoto-san!

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.250
More research?

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:22.620
Yeah. I was wondering why 
gemstones are so expensive.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:24.020
Huh?

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:29.050
Unlike minerals and rocks, 
I'm sure gemstones are expensive

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:32.130
because they're processed in all kinds 
of ways to increase their beauty.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.550
Seigi-kun, have you ever been 
to a mineral show?

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:40.440
I went to hero shows as a kid...

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:44.480
"Mineral" is just a catch-all 
for stones and the like.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.400
So... it's a rock show?

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.810
Yeah, a rock exhibition and sale.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.440
How much do you think this is worth?

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:55.240
Maybe four million?

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.500
Try 24 million.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.870
T-Twenty-four million?!

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:04.740
An object's worth is determined 
by supply and demand, right?

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:09.130
If there are fewer objects than people 
who want them, their price goes up.

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:12.480
So this one's extremely rare.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.470
Mineral shows are fun because 
you get to see things like this.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:19.140
There's one coming up in Shinjuku.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.420
Shinjuku...

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:25.270
<i>Invite her to go with you.</i>

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:26.650
<i>"Let's go together."</i>

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:27.920
<i>"Let's go."</i>

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.070
Want to go together, Seigi-kun?

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:32.600
I do!

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:36.930
Then I'll text you the details later. 
Can I get your number?

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.200
Sure!

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:53.210
I'm back!

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:05.850
I didn't see you!

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:10.230
I don't mind if you dance or sing.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.690
Don't worry.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.990
<u>Episode 3</u>
<b>Insight of the Cat's Eye</b>

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:51.250
Oh, right.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:54.120
I finally got it. It was the last one.

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:56.330
Good work.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:04:03.000
But today's client, Satomura-sama, 
just called to cancel their appointment.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:03.800
What?

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:07.890
We'll definitely have leftovers.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:11.100
<b>Milk</b>

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:11.100
I guess I'll make milk jelly.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.000
Milk... what?

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:19.610
A child?

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:24.490
<b>Menu</b>

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:24.490
<b>Display</b>

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.470
Maybe they've mistaken us for someplace else.

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:24.490
Let's let them in.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.080
Good—

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:31.360
H-Hello.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.570
Good day to you.

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:35.040
Oh... G-Good day.

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:38.400
Are you all by yourself?

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.950
If you're lost, there's a police box nearby. 
Shall we go together?

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:45.330
I'm sure your mom and dad 
are worried about you.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:47.760
This is a jeweler's, right?

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:51.310
I came because I'd like 
to speak with a jeweler.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:53.030
Alone?

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:57.070
Is that not allowed?

00:04:57.070 --> 00:05:00.100
This isn't the kind of place 
children come by themselves.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:03.120
I'm not a child. I'm a customer.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.750
Please excuse us.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:07.720
Welcome to Étranger.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:11.790
I'm the owner. My name is Richard.

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:15.370
And this is Seigi. 
He helps out around the shop.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:19.880
How did you learn about this place?

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:21.970
It's a secret.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:26.580
Would you mind telling us your name?

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:32.140
I don't have to give my name when 
I go shopping at a clothing store.

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:34.310
You're quite right.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:36.290
Please, come in.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:47.030
Seigi, prepare something to drink.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:51.210
All we have for kids is milk.

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.870
I'd like warm milk.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:56.980
I don't take sugar, but I'd like it sweet.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:57.840
What?

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:01.150
Sweet without sugar? 
Are you trying to be clever?

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:02.370
Seigi.

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:04.670
Understood.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:10.190
Now, why have you come to see a jeweler?

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:13.060
I'd like one of these gemstones.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:22.620
This is a chrysoberyl cat's eye.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:24.840
Yes, it's a cat's eye.

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:27.590
I have money.

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:31.730
I saved up my New Year's money, 
so it's in my name.

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:33.620
You have a passbook?

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:37.500
That might help us identify him. 
Let's take a look.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.960
I can't show it to a stranger.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:43.120
Seigi, don't force him to do anything.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:49.470
But we can't just do nothing, 
and I'm sure his parents are worried.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:53.140
I have an idea.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:56.760
Please mind our customer.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:57.850
Me?

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:00.860
If you'll excuse me,
I'll go get the gemstones.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:11.530
Now... Want to play, Mr. Won't-Give-His-Name?

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:12.750
No, that's too long...

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:15.550
Mr. Smart Aleck! No, too hard to say...

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:17.840
Then... Oh, I've got it! Mr. John Doe—

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.010
My name is Hajime.

00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:19.810
Huh?

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:22.390
But I won't tell you my family name.

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:25.130
Fine. Nice to meet you, Hajime-kun.

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:31.720
All right. What shall we play, Hajime-kun?

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.830
Tag? Hide-and-seek?

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:36.950
I don't play such childish games.

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:40.560
Childish? But you are a child.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.570
More importantly, where's my drink?

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:45.900
Coming right up, sir!

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:52.240
Hajime-sama, would you help me select 
some snacks to go with your beverage?

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.810
Are you trying to bribe me now?

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:57.780
You know some pretty grown-up words...

00:07:57.780 --> 00:07:59.990
There's no point in flattering me.

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:02.660
I won't say anything I don't mean to.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:11.490
Leaf pies, melon jelly, 
red bean jelly, baumkuchen...

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:13.580
I'd like some baumkuchen, please.

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:15.140
Very well.

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:17.930
Oh, actually...

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:24.730
I'll have that.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:30.250
Since you don't take sugar, 
I put honey in your milk.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:33.240
I love honey milk.

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:41.790
It's good.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:43.910
Thank you.

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:48.650
Just between you and me, 
the owner loves sweet things.

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:51.630
He turns into a monster 
whenever we run out.

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:53.830
Roar!

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:58.210
That's not funny at all.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:04.890
This is very good.

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:07.370
I like it.

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:09.650
I'm glad to hear that.

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:12.210
Thank you for waiting.

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:14.530
I've brought you the cat's eyes.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:19.050
These are apatite cat's eyes.

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:22.700
These are tourmaline cat's eyes.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:26.350
What? They're both cat's eyes?

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:27.790
Yes.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:33.530
A mineral called rutile inside the gemstone

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:35.970
gleams like the eyes of a cat
when it reflects light.

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:40.280
This light effect called chatoyancy 
is what makes a cat's eye.

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:47.730
So it's similar to how cats can have white fur
even if they're of different breeds?

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.100
Good for you.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:55.990
When I was your age, I thought someone 
had drawn the effect with a white pen.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:59.210
Do you like any of these gems?

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:05.870
I want one just like this one.

00:10:06.590 --> 00:10:09.250
There's no point if it's different.

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:15.480
If Milk were here, 
this wouldn't be happening...

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:16.690
Milk?

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:19.360
Never mind.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:22.260
Is that a cat's name?

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:25.220
Come to think of it, on his bag...

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:29.730
He's also looking for a cat's eye.

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:32.980
English uses the same phrase
to refer to an actual cat's eye.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:35.580
Cats have two eyes.

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:38.240
Is that why you need a matching stone?

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:45.120
Is it a cat with eyes the color 
of chrysoberyl cat's eyes?

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:54.000
Does the reason you came here have 
something to do with that cat, Hajime-kun?

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:57.970
You don't have to tell us 
if you don't want to.

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:02.680
But when I see a troubled customer,
 I want to help them.

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:12.670
Milk was a stray cat.

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:17.820
We adopted him when I began 
attending grade school.

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:22.450
Milk has strange powers.

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:31.960
He once kept us from going on a drive.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:37.460
<b>Breaking News: </b>Mountain Cliff Collapses, 
Earth Spilling Into Roadway<b></b>

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:35.650
While watching the news, 
we saw that there'd been a landslide

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:37.460
on one of the roads we'd planned on driving.

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:42.470
There was also the time 
Milk kept biting Dad's arm.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:45.700
When we went to the hospital, 
they discovered he was sick.

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:52.270
Even Mom and Dad said Milk saved us.

00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:55.790
So it's a cat that can predict bad things.

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:57.540
Yeah.

00:11:57.540 --> 00:12:02.820
Milk always stares at us
 when we leave the house.

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:08.340
Mom says he's watching over us.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:15.880
But Milk is gone now, 
and my mom is in the hospital.

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:16.780
What?

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:18.770
She's going to have a baby.

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:22.690
So we need his protection.

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:27.720
Dad gave me this gemstone 
to take Milk's place, but...

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:33.860
Earlier, you said that Milk was gone.

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:36.520
How did that come to pass?

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.200
My dad...

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:52.540
Milk? He must be around here somewhere.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:55.020
I'm sure he'll come back soon enough.

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:59.980
If there was some reason for it, 
he could tell me.

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:02.860
He thinks I can't be of any help.

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:05.590
He's a liar...

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:09.680
I hate him!

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:24.740
Excuse me.

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:32.560
I believe I understand now.

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:37.330
You're looking for a second gemstone 
to stand in for Milk, yes?

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:41.360
That's right. I won't rely on my dad.

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:44.010
I have to protect my family.

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:52.010
Having a dad like that is hard.

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:56.850
He doesn't know what he did was wrong.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:14:00.200
He doesn't know how he's hurting you.

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:02.860
He's the worst.

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:06.740
That kind of parent... is the worst.

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:11.220
Seigi?

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:15.160
You have no right to say that!

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:18.270
What do you know?

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:20.810
My dad is really busy!

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:23.670
He just went crazy from working too hard!

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:28.720
Maybe he took Milk away because he was dying,

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:32.930
and he didn't want Mom to worry about it!

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:35.520
You jerk!

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:44.480
Sorry.

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:52.930
Is this a gemstone of good or bad 
fortune for you, Hajime-sama?

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:59.300
Since ancient times, cat's eyes have 
been prized as protective gemstones.

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:03.580
They were thought to be 
gemstones of misfortune in Europe,

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:08.960
but in Japan and the rest of Asia, 
they're believed to bring good luck.

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:14.240
Just as you're searching for a 
gemstone to protect your family,

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:20.440
perhaps your family has imbued 
this one with their love for you.

00:15:21.570 --> 00:15:24.620
Gemstones are mirrors 
that reflect their owners.

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:27.010
They understand how we feel.

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:29.430
No matter the place or time,

00:15:29.430 --> 00:15:33.660
there isn't anyone who gives a protective 
charm to someone they don't care about.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:38.780
Perhaps it would be best to 
speak with your father again.

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:51.050
Hajime!

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:53.630
Dad?

00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:55.510
What? Your dad?

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:57.220
How?

00:15:57.730 --> 00:16:00.600
Richard-san called me.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:02.690
Richard-san, I'm so sorry.

00:16:03.510 --> 00:16:09.940
Yasaka-sama purchased 
that chrysoberyl cat's eye.

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:14.200
I assumed Hajime-sama must be his son.

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:15.830
Hajime.

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:19.820
I can't believe you took that 
out of the house and did all this.

00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:20.930
But Milk...

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:23.420
You're bothering Richard-san and his shop!

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:27.590
Come on. Let's go, Hajime.

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:32.970
Excuse me.

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:37.560
Please hear Hajime-kun out.

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:39.040
What?

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:40.450
It's fine.

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:44.070
Dad's always like this.

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:48.270
He doesn't tell me anything, 
and he doesn't listen to me.

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:53.400
Hajime...

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:06.020
Are you familiar with a condition 
called toxoplasmosis?

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:07.330
No.

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:12.240
Stray cats carry a parasite 
called toxoplasma.

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:16.620
It can make pregnant women sick 
if they come in contact with it.

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:20.020
It's because Milk was a stray cat?

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:27.090
Yeah, so I'm having a secretary from 
my office take care of him to be safe.

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:29.560
Why didn't you tell me?

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:34.110
I planned on bringing him back home 
as soon as the baby was born.

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:36.060
So you lied to me?

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:41.440
I didn't tell you the truth because 
I thought it would worry you.

00:17:41.440 --> 00:17:42.620
Huh?

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:46.620
But it seems I only made you worry more.

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:49.390
I'm sorry, Hajime.

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:58.570
Did you ask Richard-san about this gemstone?

00:17:58.570 --> 00:18:02.470
Chrysoberyl cat's eyes 
come in a variety of colors,

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:06.350
but there is a standard for 
particularly high-quality gemstones.

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:11.080
The center band must be 
a clear, beautiful white.

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:14.890
And the rest of the stone must 
be a golden honey color.

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:21.240
We call this particular kind of stone 
a "honey and milk" cat's eye.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.430
Honey and milk...

00:18:24.820 --> 00:18:28.080
Honey milk is your favorite, isn't it?

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:33.390
I bought it because I thought it would 
protect you and make you happy.

00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:39.360
Dad...

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:42.070
I have a request.

00:18:42.590 --> 00:18:43.970
What is it, Hajime?

00:18:44.420 --> 00:18:47.180
Promise you won't lie anymore.

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:52.310
All right. I promise.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:56.690
I won't lie anymore.

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:02.870
Pinky promise, hope to die.

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:07.780
Swallow ten million needles if you lie.

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:09.910
What? Ten million needles?

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:12.710
It's fine as long as you don't lie. 
Should be easy, right?

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:18.370
This is a real, super-duper promise, okay?

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:20.260
Yeah, super-duper.

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:21.240
You super promise?

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:22.420
I super promise.

00:19:27.170 --> 00:19:29.980
Anyway, I'm surprised you knew all that.

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.400
Did you just happen to remember?

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:34.610
What are you talking about?

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:37.280
The gemstone you sold and the buyer.

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:39.390
Of course I remember.

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:41.700
But not every single one, right?

00:19:42.940 --> 00:19:44.140
You don't mean...

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:50.790
That honey and milk cat's eye is 
from Sri Lanka, 36.42 carats.

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:58.010
It was the largest and most beautiful 
chrysoberyl cat's eye I've ever handled.

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:00.350
I underestimated you.

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:06.600
Didn't he say he bought that 
gemstone for Hajime-kun?

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:09.530
What's it worth? Around a million yen?

00:20:09.530 --> 00:20:11.720
More than ten million.

00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:13.390
T-Ten million?!

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:16.630
Perhaps he wanted to leave 
something for his son

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:19.730
just in case something happened.

00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:21.870
A gemstone?

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:26.390
You're familiar with asset 
management, aren't you?

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:28.350
Of course.

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:32.030
Small, light, portable at a moment's notice,

00:20:32.030 --> 00:20:34.410
and exchangeable for cash in any country.

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:37.060
Rare gemstones are valuable.

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:42.050
The mineral show...

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:45.380
Are you interested in mineral shows?

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:48.760
Well, a little.

00:20:49.110 --> 00:20:53.700
In European culture, accessories are 
passed down from generation to generation.

00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:55.480
Was it like that for you, too?

00:20:56.090 --> 00:20:57.060
I suppose.

00:20:57.570 --> 00:21:02.890
You can feel the parent's love in a gemstone 
passed down from parent to child.

00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:05.910
It's a lovely thing.

00:21:07.400 --> 00:21:10.160
Love and compatibility are different.

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:12.620
<b>Milk</b>

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:18.540
Seigi, when you get the chance, 
please buy a special cheesecake.

00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:24.050
I was very much looking 
forward to enjoying it.

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:27.300
Thanks in advance.

00:21:28.190 --> 00:21:33.140
By the way, you said you'd make 
something with the leftover milk.

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:35.850
Oh, you mean the milk jelly?

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:40.860
What kind of food is milk jelly?

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:46.860
You really are the king of sweets. 
You can't <i>not</i> try it.

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:49.740
Who's the king of sweets?

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:54.260
There's not much left here, 
so I'll buy some more.

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:58.420
You'll never get a raise at this rate.

00:21:59.220 --> 00:22:00.920
I prefer pudding.

00:22:01.220 --> 00:22:02.060
Huh?
